import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse('{"title":"Retro — conv_bn_fold ships: DEFAULT takes a machine-minted composite","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Retro — `conv_bn_fold` ships: `DEFAULT` takes a machine-minted composite","type":"retro","date":"2026-10-19T00:00:00.000Z"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/retros/minted-composite-default.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/retros/minted-composite-default.md"}'),a={name:`graphopt/project/retros/minted-composite-default.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="retro-—-conv-bn-fold-ships-default-takes-a-machine-minted-composite" tabindex="-1">Retro — <code>conv_bn_fold</code> ships: <code>DEFAULT</code> takes a machine-minted composite <a class="header-anchor" href="#retro-—-conv-bn-fold-ships-default-takes-a-machine-minted-composite" aria-label="Permalink to “Retro — conv_bn_fold ships: DEFAULT takes a machine-minted composite”">​</a></h1><p><strong>Follows</strong>: <code>premise-anchored-derivability.md</code> (the anchored <code>derivable</code> leg), <code>binding-env-cap.md</code> (the terminating gauntlet), <code>fold-cost-single-source.md</code> (the pay leg), <code>0f5fc15</code> (the closure gate&#39;s bounded-footprint forgiveness) — the conv+BN composite&#39;s gauntlet is fully green: <code>usable=True</code> on the measured corpus. <strong>Commit</strong>: <code>445d1c7</code> (the ship) + this commit (retro + ledger).</p><h2 id="the-question" tabindex="-1">The question <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-question" aria-label="Permalink to “The question”">​</a></h2><p>Does <code>DEFAULT</code> take a machine-minted <code>syn_*</code> composite, or is admission for authored family members only? The honest tension the task named: the composite&#39;s premise family — <code>batch_norm_expand</code> + the four <code>conv_channel_*</code> anchors — is itself <strong>enabled-but-opt-in</strong> (anchors refused at truth-starvation, the expand at typed-pay). If the composite enters <code>DEFAULT</code> while its parents don&#39;t, is that coherent?</p><h2 id="the-decision-—-yes-and-the-coherence-was-already-settled" tabindex="-1">The decision — yes, and the coherence was already settled <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-decision-—-yes-and-the-coherence-was-already-settled" aria-label="Permalink to “The decision — yes, and the coherence was already settled”">​</a></h2><p><strong>Ship it, verbatim.</strong> Two precedents carry the coherence argument:</p><ul><li><code>linear_channel_to_row_scale</code> sits in <code>DEFAULT</code> while both its premises are SYMMETRY-gated opt-ins — the shipped composite edge is self-contained: its guard is the transported conjunction evaluated on its own binding, and at fire time it does <em>not</em> replay its parents. The parents&#39; exclusion reflects <em>their own</em> measured economics (closure cost, standalone pay) — a per-law account the composite does not inherit. The conv+BN case is the same shape, one level deeper.</li><li>The premise-anchored machinery was built for exactly this: the composite&#39;s <code>derivable</code> credit is premise-scoped <em>by construction</em> — &quot;derivable under the premises I was minted from&quot;, each step site-verified. Requiring the premises to also be DEFAULT members would re-conflate the two axes the anchored gate was built to separate: a premise&#39;s <em>truth</em> (unit-verified, on which the anchored proof rests) vs its <em>default-set economics</em> (the opt-in verdict).</li></ul><p>The residual candidates checked and discharged:</p><ul><li><strong>runtime correctness</strong> — the transported <code>check</code>/<code>derive</code> are closures over the <em>same</em> library parent objects the mint composed over; they resolve at fire time, not at storage. Verified: the shipped <code>CONV_BN_FOLD</code> fires on the spelled eval-mode site producing the identical fused instance (<code>dag_cost</code> 34 874.3 → 17 438.7) and declines a channel-mismatched binding.</li><li><strong>closure safety in <code>DEFAULT</code></strong> — the firing footprint is bounded (19 minted enodes + cascade ≤ 2×), measured, not a saturation blow-up; the rule fires once per guarded site — term-local, like every other shipped fold.</li><li><strong>truth</strong> — premise-anchored derivable (replayable cert, site-verified steps) + 105eq/0ne on the guarded synth region + 1eq/0ne on the real site + <code>verify=pass</code> on the lowered modules.</li></ul><h2 id="what-shipping-a-composite-means-mechanically" tabindex="-1">What shipping a composite means mechanically <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-shipping-a-composite-means-mechanically" aria-label="Permalink to “What shipping a composite means mechanically”">​</a></h2><p><code>promoted-laws.md</code>&#39;s class shipped by <em>transcription</em>: each admitted object was re-written as an <code>R(...)</code> whose <code>cond</code> was hand-verified to be &quot;exactly what compose_objects minted&quot;. That path does not scale to a depth-4 interleaved check+derive composition — a hand-flattened <code>cond</code> for it would be an <em>unmeasured twin</em>, not the admitted object. So <code>conv_bn_fold</code> introduces a second shipping class:</p><p><strong><code>mlopt_core.laws.minted</code></strong> — the verbatim path. The stored-closure records (the four <code>syn_*</code> nodes&#39; <code>law_json</code>, each carrying its <code>&quot;guard&quot;</code> spec: parent names + <code>guard_pats</code> re-expression maps) embed as data; <code>materialize()</code> replays <code>evidence._rebuild_stored</code>&#39;s semantics at import over the embedded table plus the shipped library&#39;s name table. Deliberately <em>louder</em> than the store: a parent that resolves short of declared strength — absent, cyclic, or weaker-than-declared — raises at import rather than admitting a degraded rule. A shipped object may never silently lose its guard.</p><p>The honest consequences, pinned:</p><ul><li><code>missing_hooks(conv_bn_fold) == (&quot;check&quot;, &quot;derive&quot;)</code> — the first shipped law that is not bare-record full-data. The census (<code>test_law_serialize.py</code>) gains a <strong>transported</strong> bucket keyed on <code>guard_pats</code> — the class is marked, not hidden: the guard&#39;s <em>spec</em> is data even though the hooks are code, and <code>store_object</code> re-encodes the spec faithfully on re-store (pinned round-trip test).</li><li><code>kind == &quot;axiom&quot;</code> by annotation: the <code>derivation</code> field can only name shipped rules, and the true derivation runs through three unshipped <code>syn_*</code> intermediates — and the <code>test_axiom_lemma_marker</code> premise check requires recorded names to resolve inside <code>ALL_RULES</code>, so a partial annotation would be a <em>worse</em> lie. The lineage rides <code>rule.parents</code> + the embedded records instead.</li><li><code>emit-basis</code> re-measured: <code>ALL_RULES</code> 83→84, <code>conv_bn_fold</code> reads <code>no-instance</code> like every other shape-guarded promotion (the instancer builds no site); declared split 60 axioms / 22 lemmas / 2 redundant; measured no-instance 19→20.</li></ul><h2 id="the-alternative-considered-—-a-machine-default-adjunct-set" tabindex="-1">The alternative considered — a <code>MACHINE_DEFAULT</code> adjunct set <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-alternative-considered-—-a-machine-default-adjunct-set" aria-label="Permalink to “The alternative considered — a MACHINE_DEFAULT adjunct set”">​</a></h2><p>Consulted-alongside-<code>DEFAULT</code> segregation was weighed and rejected on honesty grounds: either every recommended caller composes it (then it <em>is</em> DEFAULT membership with indirection, and the class boundary is fiction) or nobody does (then the measured evidence is stranded — &quot;admitted but unreachable&quot;). The class distinction belongs in <em>provenance</em> (<code>MACHINE_SHIPPED</code>) and on the object (<code>guard_pats</code>, <code>parents</code>), not in set membership. The one real residual that would have justified the adjunct — a guard the library&#39;s audit surfaces cannot read — is addressed by marking the class (census bucket + provenance), not by quarantining it.</p><h2 id="second-order-effects-observed-post-ship" tabindex="-1">Second-order effects observed post-ship <a class="header-anchor" href="#second-order-effects-observed-post-ship" aria-label="Permalink to “Second-order effects observed post-ship”">​</a></h2><ul><li><code>conv_bn_fold</code> in the mint base changes what <code>synthesize_rules</code> finds: the probe&#39;s fixpoint now emits <code>syn_conv_bn_fold__comm_add_0</code> first — a trivial comm-compose whose guard spec names the <em>shipped composite</em> as a parent, and whose transport correctly refuses when the composite&#39;s own premise rows are absent from the store. The probe pins its mint base to the pre-ship surface so it keeps measuring the admitted object.</li><li>The same mint re-runs deterministically (974 emitted, identical <code>syn_*</code> names across runs) — the embedded records are the measured artifact, not a sample.</li><li>Re-running the gauntlet post-ship refuses at <strong>novelty</strong> (<code>relation=duplicate</code>) — the documented signature of &quot;already admitted&quot;, identical to the promoted-laws aftermath.</li><li>The premise-anchored leg now resolves through the shipped law: <code>verify_law</code> under shipped axioms derives the mint in one step (<code>witness=(&#39;conv_bn_fold&#39;,)</code>) — the library law proving its own minted origin.</li><li>The library-side guard sweep (<code>test_guard_sweep._guarded</code> keys on <code>cond or check or derive</code>) <em>does</em> cover the transported class — <code>conv_bn_fold</code> swept 218 sites: 1 true, 217 false, <strong>0 violations</strong>. Thin acceptance is the enumeration&#39;s conv-corner starvation the joint-shape work already names, not a coverage hole; the gauntlet&#39;s guarded-region sweep (105eq/0ne) remains the deeper measurement.</li></ul><h2 id="what-stays-open" tabindex="-1">What stays open <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-stays-open" aria-label="Permalink to “What stays open”">​</a></h2><ul><li>A <em>flattened</em> <code>cond</code>/<code>dspec</code> transcription of the transported guard — the composite&#39;s accepted region is a conjunction of renamed parent conds over inline-derive attrs, which the DSL can express — would restore the full-data census property. It needs a flattener (or a verified hand transcription), then a fresh gauntlet run on the twin.</li><li>The LHS carries the seed&#39;s literal attrs (<code>stride=(1,1)</code>, <code>padding=(1,1)</code>, <code>eps=1e-05</code>, <code>training=False</code>): the law&#39;s region is the default-attr eval-mode fold — narrow, honest, and the common spelling; generalizing the attr metvars is a new measurement, not a transcription detail.</li></ul><p>Gate account: <code>tests/test_minted_laws.py</code> (+9), the count pins (<code>test_laws_structure</code>, <code>test_law_serialize</code> census, <code>test_law_provenance</code> table) re-pinned at 84/285/12; focused slices green; ruff/format/ty/vulture/lint-imports/bandit/semgrep/radon clean on touched files; dev lane (<code>-m &quot;not slow&quot;</code>) run logged in GOALS.</p>`,21)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};